{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And HaShem has not given you a heart to know.</b> To recognize the kindnesses of the Holy One, blessed be He, and to cleave to Him." "<b>Until this day.</b> I heard that on that very day when Moses gave the scroll of the Torah to the tribe of Levi, as written (Deuteronomy 31) ״וַיִּתְּנָהּ אֶל הַכֹּהֲנִים בְּנֵי לֵוִי״, all Israel came before Moses and said to him: Moses our teacher, we too stood at Sinai and received the Torah and it was given to us — so why do you put your tribe in authority over it, so that tomorrow they may say to us: It was not given to you, it was given to us? And Moses rejoiced at the matter, and on this account he said to them: ״הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה נִהְיֵיתָ לְעָם וְגוֹ׳״ — This day I have understood that you are devoted and desirous of the Omnipresent."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:47.435735509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}